        "date_dead_since": null,
        "date_published": "2026-02-06T13:38:18+00:00",
        "description": "<p>Gigacode is an experimental, just-for-fun project that makes OpenCode's TUI + web + SDK work with Claude Code, Codex, and Amp.<p>It's not a fork of OpenCode. Instead, it implements the OpenCode protocol and just runs `opencode attach` to the server that converts API calls to the underlying agents.<p>We build this to scratch our itch of being able to rapidly switch between coding agents based on the task at hand. For example, we find that:<p>- Claude Code is the best executor & fast iterator\n- Codex (high) is the best for complex or long-running tasks\n- OpenCode for fine-tuned, do-exactly-as-I-say edits<p>I personally believe that harnesses matter almost as much as the models in 2026. OpenCode lets you swap out models already, but the CC & Codex harnesses + system prompts make a big difference in practice.<p>Under the hood, this is all powered by our Sandbox Agent SDK:<p>- Sandbox Agent SDK provides a universal HTTP API for controlling Claude Code, Codex, and Amp\n- Sandbox Agent SDK",
        "id": 4752787,
        "language": "en-US",
